#!/bin/sh
# DS-212j: compressed swap in RAM (zram), used before the swap on the disks (md1).
# Swap on md1 lives on the very disks that hibernate: a sleeping process whose pages had
# been swapped out there (copyparty: ~26 MB after the media migration) woke the disks up
# with every swap-in. zram (priority 100) takes the swap-outs; md1 (default priority) is
# only used when zram is full. zswap (a compressed cache in front of disk swap) is
# disabled: in front of zram it would only compress twice.
# usage: ds212j-zram start|stop|reclaim
#   reclaim: move the pages already on the disk swap back into RAM/zram (swapoff +
#   swapon), only if MemAvailable stays above 64 MB afterwards
set -eu
SIZE=${ZRAM_SIZE:-96M}
ALGO=${ZRAM_ALGO:-lzo-rle}
case "${1:-}" in
start)
	[ -w /sys/module/zswap/parameters/enabled ] && echo N > /sys/module/zswap/parameters/enabled
	[ -e /sys/block/zram0 ] || modprobe zram num_devices=1
	if ! grep -q '^/dev/zram0 ' /proc/swaps; then
		echo 1 > /sys/block/zram0/reset 2>/dev/null || true
		echo "$ALGO" > /sys/block/zram0/comp_algorithm 2>/dev/null || true
		echo "$SIZE" > /sys/block/zram0/disksize
		mkswap -q /dev/zram0
		swapon -p 100 /dev/zram0
	fi
	;;
stop)
	if grep -q '^/dev/zram0 ' /proc/swaps; then
		swapoff /dev/zram0
		echo 1 > /sys/block/zram0/reset
	fi
	;;
reclaim)
	avail=$(awk '/^MemAvailable:/{print $2}' /proc/meminfo)
	for sw in $(awk 'NR>1 && $1 !~ /zram/ {print $1}' /proc/swaps); do
		used=$(awk -v d="$sw" '$1==d {print $4}' /proc/swaps)
		[ "${used:-0}" -gt 0 ] || continue
		if [ $((avail - used)) -gt 65536 ]; then
			swapoff "$sw" && swapon "$sw" && echo "$sw: ${used} kB moved back into RAM/zram"
		else
			echo "$sw: ${used} kB in use, not enough free memory to move it back (${avail} kB available)"
		fi
	done
	;;
*)
	echo "usage: $0 start|stop|reclaim" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
